{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "scriptId": "pl-07-successive-traders-price-chains",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Successive Traders and Price Chains",
    "description": "Track an article through manufacturer, wholesaler, retailer and later buyers as each stage adds a profit or loss multiplier.",
    "teachingApproach": "Present each trade as a multiplier in a visible chain. Move forward, reverse the chain, mix profit and loss, solve a missing stage, include expenses before the first trade, and finish with buy-back and three-stage capstones.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 28,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 12, Profit and Loss. Approved scope: Teach a price chain as successive multipliers: each trader’s selling price becomes the next trader’s cost price. Cover two- and three-hand transactions, recovering the first cost from the final price, finding a missing trader profit when overall rise is known, chains containing a loss at one stage, and reverse-working through the chain. Distinguish percentage profit on each trader’s own cost from percentage change relative to the original cost. Use compact multiplier chains such as ×1.20 ×1.25 ×1.10."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn successive traders and price chains.\n\nA table leaves a manufacturer, then a wholesaler, then a retailer. Every seller starts from the price paid to the previous seller, so each percentage changes the base for the next one.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "When an item passes from one trader to the next, each selling price becomes the next person's cost price. So the percentages multiply in a chain.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Manufacturer cost ₹1000.\nSells at 20% profit → ₹1200.\nWholesaler sells at 25% profit → 1200×1.25 = ₹1500.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
